Adblock works on windows and it can catch arbitrary patterns such as */ad/* 
or */ads/* or indeed http://ads.* which a hosts file won't catch.

The other main difference is that a blocking hosts file can leave some 
websites looking kind of empty: you may have to search a long time to find 
the actual content. Adblock will usually succeed in removing the images and 
frames entirely.

Filtered items are blocked before they load, and it is easy to turn off if 
you actually want to see the adverts.

There is also another Firefox plugin which downloads the Adblock rules 
automatically from some central system, but I haven't tried that: I have a 
fairly short block list as I only want to block the adverts which annoy me, 
not every advert.


